Z||000000||TRL46202||07-09-2001||09:24 AM||||Did some engine work rebuild/cleanup and noticed that the hard flat plastic housing that runs between the upper and lower plenum on both sides (2.8 V6) was in bad shape and needed replacing. I used 1/2in spiral looms (ones you get at any auto parts store) and placed that inside 1in loom to double the thickness. My question is, will the looms withstand the heat or does anyone know of a different material.<P>Thanks! Tom||||reg||1
Z||000001||chester||07-09-2001||09:58 AM||||Make sure its high temp loom.  I used regular off the shelf loom and it made nice streaking effects as it melted away!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P><BR>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">    <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension<p>[This message has been edited by chester (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||1
